.TH "GLESHA-CATALOG" "1" "" "glesha" "User Commands"
.nh
.ad l
.SH NAME
glesha\-catalog \- discover, open, and synchronize catalogs
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBglesha catalog\fR ACTION [SET] [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A catalog records the snapshots and files of a set. It is kept in local state and, unless the set is local\-only, encrypted on a remote. These actions manage catalogs; they never restore files.
.PP
The options each action accepts are listed with it.
.SH ACTIONS
.TP
.B sync [SET]
Without SET, search the remotes for sets and download their catalog metadata. No passphrase is needed. \-\-all is the same as giving no SET. With SET, merge remote changes into the local catalog and publish local changes. This writes to the catalog remote. Options: \-\-all, \-\-from, \-\-to, \-\-catalog\-passphrase\-file.
.TP
.B unlock SET
Decrypt the downloaded catalog of SET so that history, browse, and restore can read it. Makes no cloud requests. Requires the catalog passphrase; archives stay encrypted. Options: \-\-catalog\-passphrase\-file.
.TP
.B resolve SET
Without options, show the metadata that differs between the local and remote catalogs of SET. With \-\-keep, settle the differences using local or remote values. With \-\-authority, make the catalog on REMOTE the authoritative one. Both histories are preserved. Options: \-\-keep, \-\-authority, \-\-assume\-yes, \-\-from, \-\-to, \-\-catalog\-passphrase\-file.
.TP
.B pull SET
Replace the local catalog of SET with the remote catalog. The previous local catalog is kept. Options: \-\-from, \-\-to, \-\-catalog\-passphrase\-file.
.TP
.B push SET
Publish the pending local catalog changes of SET to its catalog remote. Options: \-\-from, \-\-to, \-\-catalog\-passphrase\-file.
.TP
.B reconcile SET
Merge the local and remote histories of SET when they do not conflict. Options: \-\-from, \-\-to, \-\-catalog\-passphrase\-file.
.TP
.B abandon SET
Discard the local work of the pending operation of SET. The catalog and remote objects are kept; spooled chunks may be deleted.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-all
Same as sync without SET.
.TP
.B \-\-keep local|remote
Settle conflicts using local or remote values.
.TP
.B \-\-authority REMOTE
Make the catalog on REMOTE authoritative.
.TP
.B \-\-assume\-yes
Answer yes to all confirmations.
.SS Remote options
.TP
.B \-\-from REMOTE...
Search or access only REMOTE.
.TP
.B \-\-to REMOTE...
Limit bucket access to REMOTE.
.PP
REMOTE... takes a comma\-separated list and may be repeated. If \-\-from or \-\-to is given, no other remote is accessed.
.SS Passphrase options
.TP
.B \-\-catalog\-passphrase\-file FILE
Read the catalog passphrase from FILE ('\-': stdin). Without this option, GLESHA_CATALOG_PASSPHRASE or a hidden prompt is used.
.PP
The global options described in glesha(1) are also accepted.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
glesha catalog sync \-\-from b2
glesha catalog unlock ID
glesha catalog sync docs
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR glesha (1),
.BR glesha\-history (1),
.BR glesha\-list (1)
